437 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 289 0 R
/E (A colonoscopy is a test where a small, soft tube with a camera is put into your rectum and colon. You will lie on your side or your back. The doctor will guide the tube through your colon and use the camera to look inside. This test is important to help the doctor see the tumor and take small pieces of tissue for testing.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
438 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 289 0 R
/E (A biopsy is a test where the doctor takes a small piece of tissue or cells from the body to check for cancer. The tissue might be collected during a colonoscopy. A doctor at the laboratory will look at the tissue under a microscope to check for cancer cells. This helps doctors make the diagnosis.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
439 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 289 0 R
/T (WHAT TESTS AND PROCEDURES WILL I HAVE? )
/E (WHAT TESTS AND PROCEDURES WILL I HAVE? )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
440 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 289 0 R
/E (Your doctor will order some tests and procedures to better understand what is happening in your body and how to help you. These tests might be done before starting treatment to help stage the cancer, or during treatment to monitor treatment effects.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
441 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 289 0 R
/E (Blood tests may be done many times during your treatment. The nurse will use a needle to take a small amount of blood. The blood test will check if your kidneys and liver are working properly and if your blood counts are normal. This is especially important before and after receiving chemotherapy. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
442 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 289 0 R
/E (The day before your colonoscopy, you can only drink clear liquids like water and broth. You will also take medicine to clean out your colon. During the procedure, you might be given medicine to help you relax and sleep. The procedure usually takes about 30 to 60 minutes.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
