497 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 293 0 R
/E (A colostomy is when the surgeon makes a small opening in your stomach called a stoma. The surgeon will connect your colon to this opening. Waste from your body will leave through this opening into a small bag on the outside of your body, instead of passing through your rectum. This bag is called a colostomy bag.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
498 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 293 0 R
/E (For some patients, the colostomy is temporary. The opening will be closed after your colon has healed. For other patients, the colostomy may be permanent. Your doctor will tell you if you need a colostomy and whether it will be temporary or permanent. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
