/S /P
/P 293 0 R
/E (It is normal to have difficult feelings about a colostomy. Many patients feel sad or worried about how their body looks and feels after surgery. It may take some time to be comfortable with the changes in your body. There are many people you can talk to about how you are feeling, like social workers, psychologists, your nurse or doctor, or other patients. Talking to others about the changes you are going through can help.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [12]
>>
