/P 294 0 R
/T (WHAT IS CHEMOTHERAPY? )
/E (WHAT IS CHEMOTHERAPY? )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
520 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 294 0 R
/E (Chemotherapy is a medicine that kills cancer cells or stops them from growing. Chemotherapy can be used before surgery to shrink the tumor, after surgery to kill any cancer cells that may be left, or when the cancer has spread to other parts of the body.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
521 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 294 0 R
/E (Chemotherapy medicine is usually given through a needle into your vein. This is called an intravenous infusion, or an IV. You will sit or lie down while the medicine drips slowly into your vein through a small tube. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
522 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 294 0 R
/E (Other chemotherapy medicines come as pills that you swallow. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
